From ed12abd7a0a528040a9edf65daee228cc2d77160 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:53:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/17] feat(mcp): require --confirm for destructive tools over
 MCP

The command reference says --confirm is required for destructive tools,
but only the agent CLI enforced it: over MCP, insight-delete ran without
the flag (friction report P20, calls #101-#105).

exec now refuses a call to a tool annotated destructiveHint unless it
carries --confirm, on every surface. The refusal says nothing ran and
gives the exact command to re-run. A caller that confirms destructive
calls another way can still pass requireDestructiveConfirmation: false.
Connected (gateway) tools that do not declare themselves non-destructive
count as destructive, which is the MCP default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
